   "text": "I read the macrocycle region by region and wrote the SMILES as one ring running around it. The stereocentres were assigned from the wedges and hashes as drawn.\n\n**Ring sequence, starting at the amide N on the meta-substituted benzene:**\n1. The aryl NH is acylated by a succinyl linker, NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)\u2013.\n2. Next comes N-methyl-leucine with an isobutyl side chain. The wedge on its \u03b1-carbon gives the L-like configuration.\n3. Then a phenylalanine NH, with a benzyl side chain on a hashed bond.\n4. Then N-methyl-isoleucine, with a sec-butyl group, a wedged methyl and a hashed N-methyl bond.\n5. Then glycine NH\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O).\n6. That carbonyl connects to N(Me)\u2013CH2CH2\u2013CH=CH\u2013C(=O)\u2013O, with the double bond drawn cis (Z).\n7. The ester O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2 is followed by C(=O)C(=O) and then the pipecolic acid nitrogen, a six-membered piperidine ring.\n8. The pipecolic C2 carries a wedged C(=O)\u2013O ester to a benzylic CH, which has a hashed CH2CH2 bond to a 3,4-dimethoxyphenyl group.\n9. That benzylic CH is attached to the meta position of the benzene ring where the sequence began.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** working through each wedge or hash gave the following.\n- Leu \u03b1-carbon: `[C@@H]`.\n- Phe \u03b1-carbon: `[C@H]`. By this reading it is the D-configuration, but I followed the drawing.\n- Ile \u03b1-carbon: `[C@@H]`, and Ile \u03b2-carbon: `[C@@H]`.\n- Pipecolic C2: `[C@H]`.\n- Benzylic ester carbon: `[C@H]`.\n\nI checked ring closures and branch counts by hand. The aryl ring closes with the nitrogen meta to the benzylic carbon, and the piperidine has six members.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)NCC(=O)N(C)CC/C=C\\C(=O)OCC(C)(C)C(=O)C(=O)N3CCCC[C@H]3C(=O)O[C@H](CCc4ccc(OC)c(OC)c4)c5cccc(c5)N1"
